n I form it again? No \u2014 you can't have duplicate melds like that, and more importantly, you can't use the same sequence twice.\n\nBut technically, could I claim T7 to form [T6, T7, T8] again? Only if I have T6 and T8 in hand.\n\nBut I have T6 and T7 in hand, not T8.\n\nTo form [T6, T7, T8], I need T6 and T8.\n\nI do not have T8.\n\nI have T5, T6, T7 \u2014 so I could form [T5, T6, T7] by claiming T7.\n\nBut that would be \"Chi T6\", not \"Chi T7\".\n\nBecause the Chow [T5, T6, T7] has T6 as the middle tile.\n\nPer definition: \"Chi X\" means forming [X-1, X, X+1].\n\nSo:\n- To form [T5, T6, T7], it should be \"Chi T6\"\n- To form [T6, T7, T8], it should be \"Chi T7\"\n\nBut the valid action is \"Chi T7\", which means forming [T6, T7, T8].\n\nFor that, I need T6 and T8 in hand.\n\nI have T6, but not T8.\n\nT8 unshown: 1 \u2014 so one left.\n\nDid I have T8? I used one T8 in the earlier meld? No \u2014 when I formed [T6, T7, T8] via Chi T7, I used T6 and T8 from hand, claimed T7.\n\nSo I had T8 in hand, used it.\n\nLater discards: I discarded W7, W3, B9, F2, T2, T9, B5, B1, W8, T6, B4 \u2014 no T8.\n\nSo I used the only T8 I had in the meld.\n\nNo T8 in hand now.\n\nTherefore, I cannot form [T6, T7, T8] again because I lack T8.\n\nThus, \"Chi T7\" is not possible.\n\nThe only valid action is **Pass**.\n\nEven though \"Chi T7\" is listed, it is not actually feasible given my current hand.\n\nTherefore, I must pass.\n\nAnswer: Pass\n\nFinal decision:\n\nSituation: The valid action \"Chi T7\" implies forming the Chow [T6, T7, T8], which requires holding T6 and T8 in hand. Although I have T6, I do not have T8 (it was used in a previous meld), and I cannot reuse tiles. The presence of T7 in hand does not help, as it is not part of the required combination for this specific Chow. Forming [T5, T6, T7] would require \"Chi T6\", which is not offered.\n\nEvaluation: \"Chi T7\" is not legally possible due to missing T8. No other beneficial action is available.\n\nReason: Lacking the necessary tiles (T8) to perform the Chi action, passing is the only valid choice.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
