d W3 or B4.\n\nNow, among the number tiles, if I must discard one of T4,T5,T6,T7, it would weaken my chow potential.\n\nFor example, if I discard T4, I keep T5,T6,T7, which is good for [T5,T6,T7].\n\nIf I discard T7, I keep T4,T5,T6 for [T4,T5,T6].\n\n[T5,T6,T7] is slightly better because it's higher and connects to my existing [T6,T7,T8] meld.\n\nAlso, T4 is more likely to be discarded by others, so safer to keep T5,T6,T7.\n\nMoreover, I have T4 in hand, and unshown T4:2, so not rare.\n\nBut for my hand, keeping T5,T6,T7 gives me a better chance for a high-scoring hand.\n\nAdditionally, if I can form [T5,T6,T7], then I have two bamboo chows: [T5,T6,T7] and [T6,T7,T8], which are shifted by one, so could contribute to \"Pure Shifted Chows\" if I have another such pair, but I may not.\n\nBut at least it's a strong foundation.\n\nI also have B4 and W3, which are dead.\n\nF3 and J3 are live but hard to use.\n\nSo the best discard is probably W3, as it's completely isolated.\n\nThen I can focus on T4,T5,T6,T7,B4,F3,J3.\n\nBut I have to discard one now.\n\nAfter discarding W3, I have T4,T5,T6,T7,B4,F3,J3.\n\nThen I can wait to form [T4,T5,T6] or [T5,T6,T7].\n\nSince I have all four, I can choose based on what is discarded.\n\nBut eventually, I need to commit.\n\nPerhaps keep all and see.\n\nBut I must discard now.\n\nAnother factor: I have F4 pung, which is 2 points for prevalent wind.\n\nIf I can get a pair, and make all chows, I can have \"All Chows\" for 2 points, plus \"Prevalent Wind\" for 2 points, plus possibly \"Self Drawn\" if I win by self-draw.\n\nBut I need more points.\n\n\"Chicken Hand\" is 8 points, which is minimum to win.\n\n\"Chicken Hand\" is defined as a hand that would otherwise be worth 0 fans, but wins, and gets 8 points.\n\nBut if I have prevalent wind pung (2 points), then it's not 0 fans, so not Chicken Hand.\n\nPatterns are summed.\n\nSo with F4 pung, I have at least 2 points.\n\nI need at least 6 more.\n\n\"All Chows\" is 2 points.\n\n\"One Voided Suit\" \u2014 I have three suits, so not.\n\n\"No Honors\" \u2014 I have honors, so not.\n\n\"Pung of Terminals or Honors\" \u2014 I have F4 pung, which is honor, so 1 point.\n\nAlready included.\n\n\"Seat Wind\" \u2014 if I have F3 pung, but I don't.\n\nSo without additional patterns, I have only 2 points from prevalent wind.\n\nI need more.\n\nPerhaps \"Mixed Double Chow\" or something.\n\nBut I need to create more value.\n\nAnother idea: discard a tile to aim for a pair.\n\nFor example, if I keep F3, and hope to draw another F3, then have a pair, but not helpful.\n\nOr keep J3.\n\nBut better to focus on the bamboo sequence.\n\nPerhaps the best is to discard W3, as it's useless.\n\nThen I have more flexibility with the rest.\n\nSimilarly, B4 is also useless.\n\nBut W3 is in a different suit.\n\nSince I have no other characters, discarding W3 might be safe and clean.\n\nB4 is in dots, and I have no other dots, so same.\n\nBut perhaps W3 is better to discard because characters are less represented.\n\nI think W3 is the best discard.\n\nFinal decision: Play W3.\n\nAnswer: Play W3"}
